  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Stacked bar chart “F. 2a.1 – Top 10 inpatient discharge diagnoses, Dec 2019 ranking” showing monthly numbers of inpatient discharge diagnoses in 2019 by category, including pneumonia, diarrhea – watery, malaria, NCDs, HIV disease, anaemias, injuries, other conditions of pregnancy and childbirth and all other specified diagnoses. Totals peak at about 490 in June and July, with malaria the largest component in May–August; March has no data.",
      "lang": "en",
      "state": "draft",
